 ## AI vision hook
 
-If both scripted retries still hold the item, an AI vision provider can transcribe the held images. The hook in `scripts/ai_vision.py` is off by default (`ai_vision.enabled` is false, `provider` is `none`). A private runner can set `CERTPASSLY_AI_VISION_ENABLED=true` and `CERTPASSLY_AI_VISION_PROVIDER=groq` to call Groq after the scripted retries. The Groq model default is `qwen/qwen3.8-27b`, temperature is 0, and the prompt asks for a strict transcription only. The API key is read from the environment variable `GROQ_API_KEY` and is never written to logs or reports. A per-run cap (`ai_vision.max_calls_per_run`, default 50) limits provider calls. Requests use a User-Agent header and send images as data URIs. Timeouts and a small number of retries apply to transient HTTP errors.
+If both scripted retries still hold the item, an AI vision provider can transcribe the held images. The hook in `scripts/ai_vision.py` is off by default (`ai_vision.enabled` is false, `provider` is `none`). A private runner can set `CERTPASSLY_AI_VISION_ENABLED=true` and `CERTPASSLY_AI_VISION_PROVIDER=groq` to call Groq after the scripted retries. The Groq model default is `qwen/qwen3.8-27b`, temperature is 0, and the prompt asks for a strict transcription only. The API key is read from the environment variable `GROQ_API_KEY` and is never written to logs or reports. A per-run cap (`ai_vision.max_calls_per_run`, default 50) limits provider calls. Requests use a User-Agent header and send images as data URIs. The Qwen model allows at most 3 images per request, so extra 400 dpi crops are stitched into one image. Timeouts and a small number of retries apply to transient HTTP errors.
 
 Committed `review/ai-reads.json` (or `review/ai-reads/QUESTION.json`) files are used when `ai_vision.use_committed_reads` is true (the default). Set `CERTPASSLY_USE_COMMITTED_AI_READS=false` or pass `--ignore-committed-ai-reads` so the live provider does the reads instead. A `hook_module` remains supported for other providers. The hook never auto-fills empty owner-correction files.
 
